Launchpad PPA publishing
========================

This package is published to the Launchpad PPA ppa:mgajda/duckdb-deb
for Ubuntu users.  This document covers what is specific to *this
package*: which series it targets, how its source packages are
produced, and how it is signed.

Target series
-------------

The PPA carries one Ubuntu series:

    noble   (24.04 LTS)

The set of series is defined by SERIES_LIST in
debian/scripts/publish-ppa.sh; adding a series is a one-line
change there.

Producing the source packages
-----------------------------

    debian/scripts/publish-ppa.sh v<X.Y.Z>-deb<N>

The script, per Ubuntu series:
  - checks out the given tag in a temporary worktree
  - sets a per-series version with dch (e.g. 1.5.2~noble0)
  - generates the orig tarball with git archive
  - builds a GPG-signed source package
    (dpkg-buildpackage -S -sa)

It then prints the dput command(s) to run.  It does not run dput
itself: the upload needs an unlocked GPG key, and keeping that
step in the maintainer's hands avoids coupling the script to
agent state.

Signing
-------

Source packages are signed with the maintainer's GPG key, whose
UID matches the Maintainer field in debian/control.  publish-ppa.sh
signs with gpg's default key unless SIGNING_KEY is exported.
